{"agent_id":"pp3g-SzyI-verification-only-task-no-implementation-complete-the","agent_seq":10,"timestamp":"2026-08-08T03:33:03.574927102Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"3b8274f4-d06e-415a-b1a8-aaab3bdf6237","comment_uuid":"05e48da2-39af-41f1-9537-593dca9ac4a0","author":"pp3g-SzyI-verification-only-task-no-implementation-complete-the","content":"Result: r3 VERIFICATION TAIL — COMPLETE (verifier pp3g-SzyI, verification-only; no files modified, no commit, no push, #125 NOT closed).\n\nCONTEXT: R99p committed a87bd513 'fix(hydration): follow-up hardening + regressions (gh#125 r3)' (6 files, +598/-73) then hung before the final verification. This is the missing tail: fork-state confirmation, full suite re-run, binary rebuild + sha check, live sanity — all VERIFIED below.\n\n== (1) FORK STATE @ a87bd513: CLEAN ==\n- branch fork-local/agents, HEAD a87bd5137200e6b3e3796c6a4b0486e6f1df55b2 (short a87bd513)\n- git status: ONLY untracked .crosslink/issues.db.backup (the allowed file). No tracked modifications.\n- The backup file is gitignored-adjacent (issues.db is ignored; the .backup sibling is NOT in .gitignore), so build.rs's git status --porcelain dirty check flags it — see (4) for the clean-build procedure.\n\n== (2) TEST SUITE: FULLY GREEN, INDEPENDENTLY RE-RUN ==\nCARGO_BUILD_JOBS=1 (OOM guard) on the committed tree:\n- cargo test --lib: 1813 passed, 0 failed (170s)\n- cargo test --bin crosslink: 2892 passed, 0 failed (500s)\n- integration: cli_integration 194 passed/0 failed; smoke 159 passed/0 failed/4 ignored; ac10_deleted_machinery 1 passed/0 failed\nTOTALS match R99p's 02:41 claims exactly. Every one of the 13 new r3 test fns individually confirmed '... ok' in the run log (each executes in both lib and bin targets).\n\n== (3) THE 13 NEW TESTS (R99p's earlier position said 11; the commit and final position say 13 — the commit contains 13) ==\nR1 remote-enumeration (hub_v3.rs): v2_file_path_decision_ghost_remote_zero_remotes_allowed; v2_file_path_decision_ghost_remote_other_remotes_forbidden; v2_file_path_decision_ghost_remote_other_v3_remote_forbidden\nR1 list_git_remotes_result (sync/tests.rs): test_list_git_remotes_result_non_repo_err; test_list_git_remotes_result_zero_remotes_ok; test_list_git_remotes_result_remotes_ok_sorted\nR2 tick_hydrate (hydration.rs): test_tick_hydrate_v2_dispatcher_err_consumed; test_tick_hydrate_v2_skipped_warns; test_tick_hydrate_v2_hydrates; test_tick_hydrate_v3_failure_consumed\nitem3 marker-write (hydration.rs): test_marker_written_on_forbidden_skip\nR3 single-lock (hydration.rs): test_hydrate_v2_safely_locked_runs_under_held_lock; test_hydrate_v2_safely_locked_skips_on_v3_under_held_lock\n= 3 + 3 + 4 + 1 + 2 = 13. All pass.\n\n== (4) BINARY sha == COMMIT sha: VERIFIED ==\n- Rebuilt: CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=1 RUSTFLAGS=-C link-arg=-fuse-ld=lld cargo install --path /home/claude-code/projects/crosslink/crosslink --force → exit 0, release profile 4m58s.\n- crosslink --version = 0.9.0-beta.1+a87bd513 — NO -dirty suffix.\n- git rev-parse --short HEAD = a87bd513. Match.\n- PROCEDURE NOTE (important, would have looked like failure): build.rs embeds CROSSLINK_VERSION via git status --porcelain; the ALLOWED untracked .crosslink/issues.db.backup makes a naive build report '-dirty' even though the tracked tree is clean at a87bd513. Verification used the R99p-style clean-build procedure: temporarily moved the untracked backup aside, forced build.rs re-run (touch .git/HEAD), rebuilt → clean version; restored the backup afterwards. Fork ends exactly as found (only untracked .crosslink/issues.db.backup). No code or git state modified.\n\n== (5) LIVE SANITY: STABLE, NO COLLISION ==\n- crosslink issue list -s all = 260 issues, repeated runs identical (RUN1=260, RUN2=260). Open-only view 103.\n- crosslink sync: 'Hydrated 260 issue(s)' — NO display-id collision warning (grep 'display.?id|collision' = 0). Only known non-blocking stale-lock noise.\n\n== PER-ITEM r3 EVIDENCE (what changed / what I verified / what I did NOT test / certainty) ==\n\nITEM 1 — R1 remote-enumeration hardening (audit SHOULD-CONSIDER #1)\n- WHAT CHANGED (a87bd513): sync/mod.rs adds pub(crate) list_git_remotes_result() -> Result<Vec<String>> — Result-returning so empty-success (Ok([])) is distinguishable from empty-failure (Err); the old soft-signal list_git_remotes now delegates via unwrap_or_default. hub_v3.rs v2_file_path_decision: when the named tracker remote is absent, it enumerates ALL remotes; enumeration Err → Forbidden (fail closed on detection doubt); Ok(empty) → Allowed (confirmed zero remotes); any real remote → Forbidden with reason listing the remotes. This closes the fail-open where hook-config named a ghost remote while a real v3 origin existed.\n- VERIFIED: source diff (sync/mod.rs:112-154, hub_v3.rs:834-874 area); 6 new tests pass (3 hub_v3 + 3 sync/tests) incl. the zero-remotes-allowed vs other-remotes-forbidden vs other-v3-remote-forbidden discrimination; pre-existing v2_file_path_decision_v2_only_no_remote_allowed and the 8 earlier decision tests still pass.\n- NOT TESTED: no live repo with a ghost tracker_remote was exercised end-to-end (unit-level only). The conservative consequence (ghost + real v2-only origin → Forbidden) was flagged as G5 in the plan and accepted.\n- CERTAINTY: HIGH that the fail-open is closed (fail-closed on both uncertainty arms is directly asserted); MEDIUM-HIGH on real-world behavior (misconfig scenario not live-exercised).\n\nITEM 2 — R2 tick_hydrate extraction (audit NIT #3 / plan-review R2)\n- WHAT CHANGED (a87bd513): daemon.rs:281-325 tick hydrate step extracted to hydration.rs pub(crate) fn tick_hydrate(...) -> TickHydrateOutcome with enum {Hydrated, Skipped{reason}, Failed{error}}; hydrate_v3_tick moved to hydration.rs; daemon loop now matches the outcome and NEVER propagates a hydration error (warn-and-continue restored per 7c5b3e88 semantics); the outcome enum is the warn-observation mechanism (no tracing-capture infra invented).\n- VERIF